<title>PHILIPPINES: Swift up on earnings expectations - brokers.</title>
<headline>Swift up on earnings expectations - brokers.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swift Food Inc, the poultry unit of RFM Corp, rose 15 centavos, or 5.77 percent, to 2.75 pesos per share by mid-session on Tuesday on expectations of better earnings this year, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Swift is up because it's a recovery story. The market expects that they will have higher earnings as a result of the increased demand during last Christmas,&quot; said Rudsend Alpay, Lippo Securities assistant vice president.</p>
